                "version": "3bd292c1476f5becb658418b70ee36153cfce830",
                "answer_guidance": "Transmission delay is unchanged because it is packet size divided by transmission rate, both fixed. Propagation delay doubles because it is cable length divided by propagation speed, and only cable length doubles.",
                "criteria": [
                  "Identify packet size and transmission rate as the determinants of transmission delay.",
                  "Identify cable length and propagation speed as the determinants of propagation delay.",
                  "Apply the stated controlled change to both quantities."
                ],
                "acceptable_variations": [
                  "The time to put the packet onto the cable stays the same; its signal travel time doubles.",
                  "Verbal proportional reasoning is sufficient; equations are optional."
                ],
                "partial_credit_guidance": "One correct effect with the other missing or wrong is partial. Both effects correct without explanation are partial and need a brief reasoning probe. If the student uses transmission to mean total delivery, clarify terminology before assigning a misconception hypothesis."
              },
